this simple-looking blob is actually a  swarm of millions of magnetic  nanoparticles the swarm is controlled by  a rapidly oscillating magnetic field  [Music]  modifying the magnetic field allows the  micro swarm to move about it can also  change direction and shape split-up  rejoin and even move through a maze  [Music]  the idea is to imitate the swarms found  in nature and animals like birds or fish  these groups of individuals together  form large shapes but they're much more  flexible in a single large creature  would be the same can be said of the  micro swarm it's strong enough to  manipulate small objects but flexible  enough to fit through narrow spaces this  technology may have medical applications  perhaps delivering drugs around the body  or acting as a contrast agent for x-rays  or ultrasound scans but although this  micro storm is pretty good at getting  through a simple maze the inside of the  human body is a much tougher challenge  tricky obstacles like fast flowing blood  cells and highly salty solutions can  complicate things so a lot more work is  needed before magnetic nanoparticles can  start swarming around inside your body  you  you
 

